What is a Polishing Line?
A Polishing Line is an integrated automated system used for continuous grinding, honing, pre‑polishing, polishing and mirror‑finishing of marble, granite, quartz and quartzite slabs. It typically comprises conveyors, multiple polishing/grinding spindles or beams, abrasive wear monitoring and compensation systems, PLC‑based controls, water spray and dust‑control units, plus optional modules such as scanners, weighing devices, waxing units or protective‑film applicators. Designed for industrial‑scale continuous processing, the line improves gloss, surface consistency, throughput and yield and can be customized according to stone type, slab thickness and automation level.
